                  <provenance type="#i"><orgName role="fmo" key="mlgbOrg_4">Canterbury, Kent.
                        Benedictine cathedral priory of Holy Trinity or Christ Church.
                        </orgName><p>'Iste liber constat Willelmo Ingram, qui erat compositus anno
                        domini MoCCCColxxviijo'. William Ingram was professed a monk of Christ
                        Church in 1484, died after 1533 (Greatrex, Register, 209). He was the
                        compiler of an inventory of 306 books from the library over the prior's
                        chapel that were repaired. These two paper volumes are his own notebooks
                        with various treatises inside on logic, etc.</p></provenance>
